# Agent SDK Monolith

## Rule

**100% of agent business logic** lives in `packages/agent-sdk`.

`apps/api/src/agents/` contains **only**:

- HTTP controllers (`POST /api/agents/:agentId/run`, review endpoints)
- Registry / loader (`agent-catalog.ts`)
- Adapters injecting Prisma, RAG, credits, storage into SDK

## Forbidden in apps/api

- Agent workflow steps with LLM calls
- Step-specific prompt templates
- `learning/feedback-handler.ts` implementations
- `if (agentId === 'cuts')` business branches

## Required per agent (SDK)

```
packages/agent-sdk/src/agents/<agentId>/
  agent.ts
  schemas/
  prompts/
  learning/feedback-handler.ts   ← mandatory
```

## Workflow kernel

`WorkflowEngine` runs in SDK — see `docs/agents/workflow-engine.md`.

## Agent IDs (canonical)

Default: `research`, `cuts`, `video_editor`  
Marketplace: `planning`, `script`, `thumbnail`, `distribution`

## When adding an agent

1. Implement in SDK first
2. Register in SDK catalog
3. Thin Nest adapter + permission keys in authz
4. Doc in `docs/agents/<agentId>/README.md`

Never create `apps/api/src/agents/<agentId>/workflow.ts` with logic.
